          deepDive: "**AかたわらB** means *besides (one's main activity) A, also doing B on the side*. 傍ら literally means *beside* (私の傍らに座る *sit beside me*): B runs **alongside** A (the book: Aをしながら、他のこと（B）もしている). A is the person's **main occupation or ongoing role** — a job, studies, child-rearing — and B is a second activity pursued in parallel **over a period of time**: 予備校で数学を教えるかたわら、小説を書いている (*he teaches math at a cram school and writes novels on the side*).\n\nConnection: **V-る + かたわら** (教えるかたわら, 経営するかたわら, 通うかたわら) or **N + かたわら**, which in the book's examples is always **Nのかたわら** (作品作りのかたわら, 育児のかたわら, りんご栽培のかたわら). The book's formula puts N directly before かたわら, but a bare noun is rare.\n\nKey points:\n- It is about **long-term, habitual activities**, not one moment: ✗テレビを見るかたわら、ご飯を食べた → ✓テレビを見ながらご飯を食べた (*ate while watching TV*).\n- The subject is an agent carrying out both activities — a person, or an organization (この動物園は動物を飼育して展示するかたわら、繁殖にも力を入れている *besides keeping and exhibiting animals, this zoo also works on breeding them*). A place merely *having two features* doesn't fit (below).\n- B often has も (繁殖にも, 製造販売もしている, エッセーも執筆されています).\n- Formal/written (formal icon): profiles, biographies, news, speeches (the listening: 大学へ通うかたわら、技術を習得するべくがんばっている *working to master the skills while attending university*).\n\nCompare:\n- **〜ながら**: neutral and covers both the moment and the long term (働きながら大学に通う *attend college while working*); かたわら is only long-term, more formal, and presents B as an extra activity.\n- **〜がてら** (Plus under #26): one outing used for a second purpose, usually movement: 散歩がてらパンを買いに行く (*pick up bread while out for a walk*).\n- **〜かたがた** (#26): N with a double purpose, formal visits: お礼かたがた伺う (*call on someone, partly to thank them*).\n- **〜一方（で）**: sets two aspects side by side, for anything, including places: 桜の名所として知られる一方、梅雨にはあじさいも楽しめる (*famous for its cherry blossoms, and you can also enjoy hydrangeas in the rainy season*). This is まとめ 問題1-4 — a shrine precinct doesn't *do* two activities, so かたわら (and かたがた, 限り) is wrong.\n\nCommon mistake: using a single occasion or a trip as A (✗出張のかたわら観光した → ✓出張がてら／出張のついでに観光した *did some sightseeing on a business trip*).\n\nJLPT tip: a job or role + ＿＿ + a second ongoing activity (〜も書いている, 〜も執筆されている) → かたわら; a walk or trip → がてら; a place with two attractions → 一方.",
