          deepDive: "**V-(ます stem) + かねる** means *can't (bring oneself to) ~, find it hard to ~*. The speaker would like to (or is expected to), but other circumstances or an inner reluctance make it impossible (the book: 〜したい気持ちはあるが…できない), and it is often chosen precisely **to avoid saying できない outright**. 理解しかねる = *I can't quite understand*; 決めかねている = *can't make up my mind*.\n\nWhere it's used:\n- **Polite refusals in business and customer service** — the classic use: 私の一存ではお答えいたしかねます (*I'm afraid I can't answer that on my own authority*), 分かりかねます, ご要望には応じかねます (*we're unable to meet your request*). It softens a *no* and sounds far more professional than できません.\n- **Polite disagreement or criticism**: 賛成しかねる, 同意しかねる (とうてい同意しかねます *I can by no means agree*), 理解しかねる, 〜とは言いかねる (値段に相応しい味とは言いかねる = おいしいとは言えない *I can hardly call it worth the price*).\n- **Indecision**: 決めかねる, 判断がつきかねる (*can't judge*: 判断がつきかねる問題 — the Check; どちらが本物か判断がつきかねる — 問題2-3), 真意をはかりかねる (*can't fathom their real intentions* — 問題1-6).\n\nIdioms with ※ notes (idiom mark):\n- **待ちかねる** *wait impatiently*: 春の訪れを待ちかねている (*can hardly wait for spring*); お待ちかねの… (*the long-awaited …*).\n- **見るに見かねて** *unable to stand by and watch*: someone's plight is so bad that you step in (同僚が手伝ってくれた *a colleague came to help*).\n\nConstraints: かねる is about will and circumstance, not ability: ✗重くて持ち上げかねる → ✓持ち上げられない (*can't lift it*). It is not used for something good you are happy to do.\n\nThe big trap — **〜かねない** looks like its negative but means *might well (something bad)*: 事故になりかねない (*it could lead to an accident*). かねる = *can't*, かねない = *could happen*. In 問題1-6 はかりかねない would mean *there's a risk they'll gauge it*, which makes no sense; はかり得る (*can gauge*) is the opposite of the intended meaning, and っぽい (*-ish*) doesn't fit.\n\nCompare **VにVない** (#63): 辞めるに辞められない (*can't quit however much I want to*) — a strong, emotional *can't*; かねる is cooler, polite and indirect.\n\nRegister: formal (formal icon), but 分かりかねます／お答えしかねます are everyday keigo. The listening: 試験の結果を…→ 電話ではお答えしかねます (*we can't give that out over the phone*).\n\nJLPT tip: the やってみよう paraphrases かねる as 〜とは言えない, まだ考えているところだ, 答えることができません and 同意できるような意見ではない — always *can't / won't*, never *must* (答えなければなりません) or *might* (考えるおそれがある).",
